  "body": "## What changed\n\nDuring playback, the simulator's stock is now cut along the move under the playhead, up to where the tool is drawn. Before this change it was cut only once each G1/G2 move had finished. This is display only: the kept stock, its checkpoints, every verdict (gouge, collision, rapid-in-stock) and what blocks the post are still cut by whole moves, exactly as before.\n\n- `camcraft-sim`: a new module, `stock_sim/partial.rs`.\n  - `partial_move` gives the travelled part of a move (lines and arcs). It uses the same `sim::point_along` that places the drawn tool, which this PR factors out of `at_seg`.\n  - `Stock::with_partial` cuts that part on a copy and returns the bricks it changed.\n  - `Script::travelled(t)` gives the playhead's fraction along the segment under it.\n- `camcraft-app`:\n  - `FieldPlay::seek_to(k, frac)` shows move `k` cut as far as `frac` on a copy of the completed-move stock. `seek_to(k + 1, 0.0)` is bit-identical to `seek(k + 1)`.\n  - `PlayIndex::position_at` gives no fraction on a connector rapid, past an op's last move or at the end.\n  - The playback worker has `request_at(k, frac)`, and `PlayFrame.frac`.\n  - The bricks of a partial cut ride the frame's patch and are re-sent once after it moves on.\n  - `Progress` and `progress` moved unchanged into `stock_play_head.rs` (400-line law).\n- `camcraft-ui`: `follow_playhead` passes the fraction.\n- Rotary and turning ops still show whole moves; the reason is in the decision file.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1516-sim-partial-move-cut.md`.\n\n**Frame cost:** this cost only applies when the playhead's fraction changes. It is one `Stock` clone (the cut layers; the mesh layer is shared) plus one sub-move sweep on the playback worker, then the existing view clone and pack. A paused playhead costs nothing new.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `camcraft-sim` lib, `stock_sim::partial`:\n  - `mid_line_stock_is_the_sweep_of_the_travelled_part`\n  - `mid_arc_stock_is_the_sweep_of_the_travelled_part`\n  - `degenerate_moves_and_fractions_cut_nothing`\n  - `the_playhead_fraction_follows_the_drawn_tool`\n- `camcraft-app --test stock_play_partial`:\n  - `the_move_in_flight_cuts_as_far_as_the_tool_travelled`: the end of the move is bit-equal to the plain seek; scrubbing back restores the start; a NaN fraction cuts nothing.\n  - `the_playhead_fraction_applies_only_to_a_move_in_flight`\n  - `the_worker_publishes_the_move_in_flight`\n- `camcraft-app --test stock_play` still passes: 7 tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green on 9bd9fcbd8 (sim, motion, app, ui suites; 9.5 min wall).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Nothing was looked at in the GUI. The worker agent cannot launch the app, so the live playback picture needs a hand test.\n- No partial cut for rotary or turning ops; they still cut whole moves.\n\nChangelog: Simulation playback removes material along a move as the tool travels, not only when each G1/G2 move ends\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1516\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
